+# The Pocket Note
+
+Ratified in Round 15. See [[Round 15 Decision Record]]. It replaces [[The Work Order HUD]].
+
+[[Otto]] can always find a sticky note in his pocket. It lists what he means to do. It is the only task surface in the game.
+
+## Ratified
+
+- **It is always on him.**
+- **It suggests. It does not order.** A task comes from a resident's request or from the note. See [[Requests]].
+- **It holds no written question.** He always has a question and a motive. They are carried by scenes and speech, and never as a line that reads as a question.
+- **It writes itself.** Nothing on it is a player action. See [[The Day Loop]].
+- **It answers one thing: what next.** What he knows is on [[The Corkboard Thread]].
+
+## Proposed, not yet ratified 🔧
+
+- **Three lines at most**, in handwriting. A line is a person, a place or a thing: "Elle, 232". "Behind 242". "Film".
+- **The first line is always the lead to the episode's object.** The others are optional.
+- **A line is added at the moment he learns something**, and struck through when it is done.
+- **One button raises it in his hand, over the scene.** The world does not pause.
+- **It never places a marker on a map.**
+- **It is written by the Suit and read by the Agent.** The work order used to carry instructions across the Shift. The note can carry them now. See [[Persona Law]].
+
+## Inherited from the work order
+
+- It stays out of the view until called. Hold-to-peek on a controller. Cursorless, per [[Commercial Frame]].
+- It is suppressed where immersion matters: cutscenes, dreams, the mind-spaces in [[The Delusions]], the bridge, [[Anna's Flat]], the underwater heart, and the climax of any pocket.
+
+## On Day 1
+
+He wakes without his name. The note's first lead is his own memory. See [[The Memory Rooms]] and [[02 SPOOL — The Job]].
+
+## 🔧 Open
+- Its test. A feel test is planned for the note together with the board that fills itself.
+- Localisation of a handwritten asset. See [[Localization Spec]].
