+# Round 15 Decision Record
+
+**Episodes, selves and the opening dream.** Decided by Coda between 13 and 14 November 2026, in three working documents outside the vault: the redesign plan for Otto's main world, the narrative redesign, and the demo plan. This note is the index of what was decided, where it now lives, and what is still open.
+
+Notes rewritten in this round are set to `draft`. Coda promotes them to `locked`.
+
+## A. Story structure
+
+| No. | Decision | Lives in |
+|---|---|---|
+| A1 | A card is an episode. It opens inside its plot and ends on the beat that matters. There is no fixed morning after Day 1, no walk to a desk for a task, and no nightly routine. | [[Episode Structure]] |
+| A2 | The story is planned as five threads. One leads each episode and one answers. | [[The Threads]] |
+| A3 | There is no work order and no handwritten note on one. Tasks come from residents, the pocket note and the place. | [[Requests]], [[The Pocket Note]] |
+| A4 | The story does not advance without the key objects. Hidden objects and side requests open the true ending fully. | [[Requests]], [[Key Items]] |
+| A5 | Each completed side request brings that resident's help into the last run and the epilogue. The standing gates stay hard. | [[Side Requests Completed]] |
+| A6 | The board fills itself. The player reads it at any time and never pins or draws. | [[The Corkboard Thread]] |
+| A7 | The board is never wrong. It may mislead by being incomplete. Mr. Vacancy cannot enter Room 202. | [[The Corkboard Thread]], [[Persona Law]] |
+| A8 | The darkroom is played once or twice in the game, and not every day. | [[The Camera]], [[Night Phase]] |
+| A9 | Otto never says that the Building is Anna. He may feel her in the Queen game. | [[Her Side]] |
+| A10 | There is always a question and a motive. It is never written as a question line. | [[The Pocket Note]] |
+| A11 | Recognitions: once a day a resident does one small thing that only Anna did. | 🔧 Not yet placed. Examples are Coda's. |
+
+## B. Mr. Vacancy
+
+| No. | Decision | Lives in |
+|---|---|---|
+| B1 | It uses Otto's journey to raise his sense, feeding him hope and breaking it, and exploiting the residents' help, so that it can consume both him and Anna. | [[Mr. Vacancy's Plan]] |
+| B2 | The truth of the plan is felt by the player, most sharply in the bad endings. No character needs to tell it. | [[Mr. Vacancy's Plan]], [[Bad Ending — Ignorant Breach]] |
+| B3 | It formed the plan in the opening dream, when the one true raven saw what Otto could become. | [[The Opening Dream]] |
+| B4 | The Agent sees shadows because it lets him. | [[Persona Law]] |
+
+## C. The opening
+
+| No. | Decision | Lives in |
+|---|---|---|
+| C1 | The game and the demo open on a chase in a dream, with no rewind. One cut serves both. | [[The Opening Dream]], [[01 №121 — Arrival]] |
+| C2 | The dream starts with falling and ends with falling. It is a tutorial and not a fight. Ravens are its only monster. | [[The Opening Dream]] |
+| C3 | The exit is a cliff set by Mr. Vacancy. Ten hits also wake him, after the lessons are given. An idle or early failure restarts from a checkpoint. | [[The Opening Dream]] |
